=head1 NAME

Paws::Evidently::Experiment

=head1 USAGE

This class represents one of two things:

=head3 Arguments in a call to a service

Use the attributes of this class as arguments to methods. You shouldn't make instances of this class. 
Each attribute should be used as a named argument in the calls that expect this type of object.

As an example, if Att1 is expected to be a Paws::Evidently::Experiment object:

  $service_obj->Method(Att1 => { Arn => $value, ..., Type => $value  });

=head3 Results returned from an API call

Use accessors for each attribute. If Att1 is expected to be an Paws::Evidently::Experiment object:

  $result = $service_obj->Method(...);
  $result->Att1->Arn

=head1 DESCRIPTION

A structure containing the configuration details of an experiment.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Arn => Str

The ARN of the experiment.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> CreatedTime => Str

The date and time that the experiment is first created.


=head2 Description => Str

A description of the experiment.


=head2 Execution => L<Paws::Evidently::ExperimentExecution>

A structure that contains the date and time that the experiment started
and ended.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> LastUpdatedTime => Str

The date and time that the experiment was most recently updated.


=head2 MetricGoals => ArrayRef[L<Paws::Evidently::MetricGoal>]

An array of structures that defines the metrics used for the
experiment, and whether a higher or lower value for each metric is the
goal.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Name => Str

The name of the experiment.


=head2 OnlineAbDefinition => L<Paws::Evidently::OnlineAbDefinition>

A structure that contains the configuration of which variation to use
as the "control" version. The "control" version is used for comparison
with other variations. This structure also specifies how much
experiment traffic is allocated to each variation.


=head2 Project => Str

The name or ARN of the project that contains this experiment.


=head2 RandomizationSalt => Str

This value is used when Evidently assigns a particular user session to
the experiment. It helps create a randomization ID to determine which
variation the user session is served. This randomization ID is a
combination of the entity ID and C<randomizationSalt>.


=head2 SamplingRate => Int

In thousandths of a percent, the amount of the available audience that
is allocated to this experiment. The available audience is the total
audience minus the audience that you have allocated to overrides or
current launches of this feature.

This is represented in thousandths of a percent, so a value of 10,000
is 10% of the available audience.


=head2 Schedule => L<Paws::Evidently::ExperimentSchedule>

A structure that contains the time and date that Evidently completed
the analysis of the experiment.


=head2 Segment => Str

The audience segment being used for the experiment, if a segment is
being used.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Status => Str

The current state of the experiment.


=head2 StatusReason => Str

If the experiment was stopped, this is the string that was entered by
the person who stopped the experiment, to explain why it was stopped.


=head2 Tags => L<Paws::Evidently::TagMap>

The list of tag keys and values associated with this experiment.


=head2 Treatments => ArrayRef[L<Paws::Evidently::Treatment>]

An array of structures that describe the configuration of each feature
variation used in the experiment.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Type => Str

The type of this experiment. Currently, this value must be
C<aws.experiment.onlineab>.



